y":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:32:52-07:00","id":994603,"title":"","content":"I always thought Sir Francis Drake was an Acanthus.<br /> <br /> I mean, not always, but if he were a mage, he would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:20:13-07:00","id":994624,"title":"","content":"Vampire: Captain<br /> There's no way in hell a vampire will pass up the chance to be in charge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:26:18-07:00","id":994625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994624#post994624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire: Captain<br /> There's no way in hell a vampire will pass up the chance to be in charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone: Captain<br /> Because every supernatural thinks he is better to lead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:36:50-07:00","id":994630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994625#post994625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone: Captain<br /> Because every supernatural thinks he is better to lead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I actually meant how each group/troupe of supernaturals would be like as a pirate crew, but if someone wants to slot individual members into specific roles, feel free.<br /> <br /> I'll try to post my concept of the Red Tide (a Vampire Pirate crew, with their ship as a vast Gargoyle, that dives beneath the waves when dawn approaches) later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:46:25-07:00","id":994668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994630#post994630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I actually meant how each group/troupe of supernaturals would be like as a pirate crew, but if someone wants to slot individual members into specific roles, feel free.<br /> <br /> I'll try to post my concept of the Red Tide (a Vampire Pirate crew, with their ship as a vast Gargoyle, that dives beneath the waves when dawn approaches) later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's definitely cooler IMO. That said, I do think a Beast would make the ideal Quartermaster for a crossover crew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:57:37-07:00","id":994679,"title":"","content":"Naturally, a crew clmposed lf a krewe would have a ship that looks like a wreck, but is in fact extremely formidable. Think the Black Pearl, but afflicted with the gold curse itself rather than its crew/krewe. Even without a haunted ship though, with their various keys and manifestations they would be able to find treasure, get to it without much need for brathing, and even control the ship from afar and set foes' ships alight or make sharks/whales/squid assault the vessels on their behalf.<br /> <br /> Seriously, on the open sea, Sin Eaters would be kings...and now I am tempted to run a pirates game with them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:01:52-07:00","id":994692,"title":"","content":"Well, if memory serves, the Seers and Diamond mages would be serving together on the same ship because of a Nameless order they joined together to defeat during the golden age of piracy. If I remember the Nameless order in question founded or controlled Nassau and they were doing something super bad wrong fun so the other wizardly lads and ladies came to wreck their day. As such, I could see the majority of the crew being Adamantine Arrow, the Pratorians and the Guardians of the Veil's more combat focused members. The Captain would probably be a mixed group of the Hegemonic, the Paternoster and the Silver Ladder. Meanwhile, the Mysterium, the Panopticon probably both have attaches there to try and manage the allocation of spoils and to screw one another over trying to acquire the spoils of the war.<br /> <br /> All in all, the boat probably barely goes anywhere, arrives several months late thanks to the crew arguing over the best courses, and as soon as they finish fighting the locals, immediately explodes as both sides of the orcale/exarch argument immediately begin trying to defeat the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:15:44-07:00","id":994706,"title":"","content":"I wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571472-navio-de-tolos-beast-hunters\">this thing</a> for Hunter, which is relevant.<br /> <br /> Also, Geist was the suggested Golden Age of Piracy- and you have to have ghost ships in a pirate game. Speaking of which, Slasher has mentioned a ghost-pirate slasher cabal which I plan to develop one day, even if in another direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:24:55-07:00","id":994710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994692#post994692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All in all, the boat probably barely goes anywhere, arrives <s>several months late</s> <b>exactly on time</b> thanks to <s>the crew arguing over the best courses</s><b> Time Magic</b>, and as soon as they finish fighting the locals, immediately explodes as both sides of the orcale/exarch argument immediately begin trying to defeat the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Damn it, that's the 3rd mutiny we <i>didn't</i> have this week!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T11:47:18-07:00","id":994720,"title":"","content":"Vampire: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/266801-bloodline-tregarthen\">I homebrewed this a while back</a><br /> <br /> Changeling: Trinica Dracken. And if you haven't read Tales of the Ketty Jay imagine Elizabeth Swan's being traumatised and broken by her time on the Black Perl and transforming herself into something like Blackbeard from Pirates of the Caribbean 4 in order to survive life on the high seas.<br /> <br /> Mage: &quot;Pirate society is free and democratic while the empires are autocratic and allow slavery&quot;. &quot;But capt'n, our society relies on the power of our guns and cutlass. Has power corrupted us into just another form oppression for the defenceless working classes. Maybe we should use our wealth to rejoin society and become abolitionists&quot;. &quot;Quite you, point that philosophising at the Seers!&quot;<br /> <br /> [Late Edit:] Hunter - the Royal navy / Spanish navy. Yes they're agents of oppressive empires, but you're pillaging murderous pirates so you don't exactly have the moral high ground and unlike those empires the various monster governments wont get round to outlawing slavery at the end of the age of piracy.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters: &quot;So do we raid a Spanish treasure fleet or shall we sail to China and see the sites&quot;, &quot;Well you only live twice, lets go to China. I don't want to get stuck into a routine.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast: Long John Silvers from Treasure Island. He takes you under his wing, is genuinely nice to you, but none of that excuses the fact he's a ruthless murdering pirate. [late edit] It also doesn't absolve him of the fact that everything horrible that happened to you is his fault, he did hire the crew of cut-throats.<br /> <br /> Princess: A swashbuckling robin hood type of Pirate who wondered in from a Disney pirate story and is determined not to let the fact she's now in an HBO pirate story wear hear down.<br /> <br /> Leviathan: The villain. All the other gamelines are busy crewing the Black Perl, while the Leviathan is Davy Jones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:21:19-07:00","id":994743,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's already a bloodline of vampire pirates (Rotgrafen). I'd nominate a Wizened Changeling as the shipwright, because of how useful it would be to have a Mobile Hollow as your pirate ship. Interdimensional hit and run attacks, with no risk of Paradox!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:33:35-07:00","id":994753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994743#post994743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's already a bloodline of vampire pirates (Rotgrafen). I'd nominate a Wizened Changeling as the shipwright, because of how useful it would be to have a Mobile Hollow as your pirate ship. Interdimensional hit and run attacks, with no risk of Paradox!</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast: a <s>girl</s> Chamber in every port. Easy resupply, shore leave, and moving yer ill gotten gains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:27:38-07:00","id":994783,"title":"","content":"It'd only work with a Makara, though. You can't really dock a ship on a floating mountain made of bones or a cramped maze of intestines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:04:33-07:00","id":994817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994783#post994783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd only work with a Makara, though. You can't really dock a ship on a floating mountain made of bones or a cramped maze of intestines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really sounds more like a challenge, than anything...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:21:42-07:00","id":994835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=994783#post994783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd only work with a Makara, though. You can't really dock a ship on a floating mountain made of bones or a cramped maze of intestines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure that's how it works; any Beast could make use of any Chamber so long as some element within it matches up with their lair traits, and if it doesn't, just form a brood with another Beast who can. Make a chamber within your ship (preferably away from where crew members sleep so they don't become less than helpful), find chambers elsewhere, and suddenly the Beast's lair is a smuggling route that works anywhere within the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:11:26-07:00","id":994886,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: The source of one too many &quot;sea dog&quot; puns. And, uh, the Lodge of the Screaming Moon would love being a &quot;ghost&quot; ship that is actually a bunch of legal privateers who prey on the worst the enemies of their nation have to offer. But mostly the puns.<br /> <br /> Deviant: Oh joy. The East India Trading Company is into Mad Science as well. Good thing we have the Fish Men they made to sink at least a few of their vessels...<br /> <br /> Demon: &quot;Pirates? We be not pirates, we be honest merchants whose ship happens to resemble the pirates ye be looking for, but as you can see, we look nothing like ye pirates...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-28-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T17:01:08-07:00","id":994955,"title":"","content":"Siren: Either they're the ones navigating the ships (Celestial Currents) or they're sinking them for various reasons (Abyssal Currents). I can definitely see a Group of Echidnals playing Davy Jones from Pirates of the Carribean (and the rest of the crew are Vodianoi, part human-fish monstrosities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T19:17:20-07:00","id":995004,"title":"","content":"Practically made for werewolf.<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded and human landlubbers would be tasked to gain blood from sailors of merchant ships so the werewolves could track them easier while at sea. Totems would be of weather or the sea, greed and other things. Weather and Elemental Gifts would let them become wildly efficient, slowing down enemies and speeding themselves, creating obstructions to any pursuers. There would probably be a much sought-after rite that allowed some sort of bonding to the ship spirit so that it would become immune to the destructive impulses of raging werewolves as if it were another raging member of the pack.<br /> <br /> Likely to be Lodge of the Reaver or the Drowned God or something where members would be called Seawolves and they offered up blood or treasure to the sea, where the lodge totem hoarded it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:59:33-07:00","id":995074,"title":"","content":"I'm just thinking how scary it would be boarding a ship that has a vampire with five dots of obfuscate. That'd be terrifying to be up against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date"