f his row boat and collects the booty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:07:18-07:00","id":995310,"title":"","content":"I imagine there's an island someplace where the Fire-Touched are trying to drown the gurihal in the hisil, and they have raiders who go out and capture as many humans and, ideally, wolf-blooded as they can to bring back and force to live there as servants and slaves to spirit gods and Pure Lords.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's what happened to Atlantis, not the mage one, or Lemuria. An entire land mass just swallowed into the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-29-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:38:48-07:00","id":995323,"title":"","content":"How about a crew of Arisen cultists and their mummy captain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:58:45-07:00","id":995332,"title":"","content":"What with the propensity towards violence on Awakening and the urge to use their, at that point, vast powers, I'd not want to be on that crew.<br /> <br /> But while it lasted a pirate crew would be a good way to hunt after lost relics. Not sure how well the mummy's powers fare on the sea, whether they have a lot of control over winds and water. Though if they were <br /> <br /> For some reason to me it seems like something the Deceived would be more likely to lean towards.<br /> <br /> Glen Cook has a sweet series of short stories about the Vengeful Dragon, a ship cursed long ago where the crew drops dead, floating eternally on fog-shrouded seas until their curse or other sorceries call upon them to act. Then they and their crew, trained to unearthly levels of ability by lifetimes of conflict and immune to any lasting harm, awaken and act as a scourge of the seas until some unknown aspect of the curse decides they're finished and puts them back to 'sleep,' where they can have fragmented dreams of being free. Sort of what I imagine a good mummy pirate crew would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:54:01-07:00","id":995393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/994585-gameline-as-pirate-crew?p=995323#post995323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a crew of Arisen cultists and their mummy captain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just what I was thinking. <br /> <br /> &quot;Ye best be careful. Ye really don't want te wake tha capt'n...&quot;<br /> <br /> They could use Kepher to track relic-laded treasure ships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:32:32-07:00","id":995451,"title":"","content":"As much as I love all the assorted ideas here, my favorite so far is a Nosferatu whose ship is just a rowboat with a coffin on it who makes it seem like he has an entire armada of ships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:46:20-07:00","id":996239,"title":"","content":"What, no Promethean Pirates, anyone? It's not like they'd be in one place long enough for the Wasteland to set in, or meeting most people long enough for Disquiet. Yet, they <i>do</i> meet lots of humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:50:51-07:00","id":996243,"title":"","content":"You need a decent amount of people to crew a ship and trips at sea could last a long time. Without few motleys you would need some humans or others on board.<br /> <br /> I suppose a centimani with a crew of Pandorans could manage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:35:32-07:00","id":996578,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Red Tide</i></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A vampiric pirate crew that operates out of a Gargoyle ship. At dawn, it dives under the waves to protect the undead crew from the sun, only to rise as the sun sets. The crew preys upon shipping and less defended outposts, using the cover of night and their own Disciplines